From: NBOSP <nbosp@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] include: make 'dri' pkg-config dependency optional for Mesa 24.x

Mesa 24.0 removed the classic DRI driver infrastructure along with the
dri.pc file it used to ship. Xwayland 24.1.x declares a hard dependency
on 'dri' in include/meson.build to locate the DRI header directory, but
that .pc file no longer exists with Mesa 24.x builds.

Upstream resolved this in Xwayland 24.2.x by querying the include path
from libdrm instead. Backport a compatible fix: try 'dri' first
(required: false), then fall back to libdrm's include dir, which already
contains the DRI headers in any Mesa 24.x sysroot.
---
diff --git a/include/meson.build b/include/meson.build
index a3b2e1f..7c4d892 100644
--- a/include/meson.build
+++ b/include/meson.build
@@ -6,7 +6,13 @@ srcs_xwayland_headers = [
 ]
 
 # DRI headers are shipped by Mesa; find them via the dri pkg-config file.
-dri_dep = dependency('dri', required : true)
-dri_inc = include_directories(dri_dep.get_variable(pkgconfig : 'dridriverdir', default_value: ''))
+# Mesa 24.0+ removed dri.pc (classic DRI was dropped). Fall back to
+# libdrm's sysroot include path, which carries the same DRI headers.
+dri_dep = dependency('dri', required : false)
+if dri_dep.found()
+    dri_inc = include_directories(dri_dep.get_variable(pkgconfig : 'dridriverdir', default_value: ''))
+else
+    libdrm_dep = dependency('libdrm', required : true)
+    dri_inc = include_directories(libdrm_dep.get_variable(pkgconfig : 'includedir', default_value: '/usr/include'))
+endif
